  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The pipeline",
      "items": [
        "one path for every frontend: the command parses, the core runs the use case, the SDK delivers, the output port writes — the TUI, print mode and the resource subcommands all sit on it",
        "the core never touches the terminal or the process: it emits events and returns a result, and the frontend decides how to render them",
        "the core is the same library in a piped run and in a TTY run — only the mode router differs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The stream contract",
      "items": [
        "stream-json is newline-delimited JSON: one versioned event per line, flushed per event, and no other text on stdout",
        "the events are start, progress, result and error, each with a sessionId; unknown event types are ignored by consumers, additive changes stay within v, a breaking change bumps it",
        "progress and prompts belong to stderr; stdout carries the result alone, so a pipe never has to strip anything"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Delivery and settling",
      "items": [
        "a 429 is not a failure of the command: the SDK retries after the backoff window and honors Retry-After, and the idempotency key makes the retry safe",
        "when the retry budget is spent, the error kind maps to exactly one exit code — 8 rate limited, 9 network or timeout, 10 server — and the error envelope still goes to stdout",
        "EPIPE ends the run quietly with 0 when the consumer closed the pipe; a broken pipe is not a crash"
      ]
    }
  ]
}